 "about_text": "Tomio Koyama Gallery is a Tokyo contemporary art gallery founded in 1996 in Saga-cho, Koto-ku, by Tomio Koyama. It has since expanded to multiple spaces across the city, currently operating in Roppongi, Tennoz and Kyobashi (opened 2024), as well as a space in Maebashi. Since its founding the gallery has been active on the international art fair circuit and has served as an early platform for young Japanese artists, helping to shape a current within Japanese contemporary art. It represents artists including Kishio Suga, Mika Ninagawa, Hiroshi Sugito and Richard Tuttle, alongside ceramic artists, and presents a program spanning established and emerging talents across nationalities and media.",
